    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0008:0003",
      "blockId": "paragraph:discussion:0008",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "This works because the style’s input type `IntegerFormatStyle/FormatInput` is a [`BinaryInteger`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/Swift/BinaryInteger) generically constrained to the [`Int32`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/Swift/Int32) type.",
      "normalizedSource": "This works because the style’s input type `IntegerFormatStyle/FormatInput` is a [`BinaryInteger`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/Swift/BinaryInteger) generically constrained to the [`Int32`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/Swift/Int32) type.",
      "sourceHash": "d0ed1de5116a7201a4420d4db1a5627527255ff9483e7212d4bfac0905586e7f",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "For example, when you format an [`Int32`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/Swift/Int32), you can use the static [`number`](formatstyle/number-4cj49.md) property that provies a `IntegerFormatStyle<Int32>`, as seen in the following example.",
      "contextAfter": "```swift\nlet perihelionDistanceToSunInKm: Int32 = 147098291\nperihelionDistanceToSunInKm.formatted(.number\n    .notation(.scientific)) // \"1.470983E8\"\n```",
